  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL; load spec.md, CLAUDE.md, god-class-ratchet.md, ADR-010.</step>
    <step order="1">BEFORE refactoring: capture the projection output for every corpus document and store it as the equivalence baseline.</step>
    <step order="2">Map seams: block projection, run projection, atom identification, table projection, numbering, part traversal.</step>
    <step order="3">Extract collaborators one seam at a time, re-running the equivalence comparison after EACH extraction.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify DI registration count unchanged.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm under 2,000 lines; delete the waiver entry.</step>
    <step order="6">Final equivalence run over the whole corpus; ArchTests, seam suite and fidelity gate green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Projection output differs for ANY corpus document after refactoring. Stop and reconcile — a difference here silently invalidates anchors, unchanged-detection and every gate number simultaneously.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the file cannot reach 2,000 lines without a new DI registration or a behavior change, surface it under §6.5.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
