  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-08-31. `ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs` 3,593 -> 1,031 via FOUR internal collaborators
    (`ComposeNumbering`, `ComposeOoxmlPrimitives`, `ComposeContentModelProjector`, `ComposeParaOffsetMapBuilder`).

    TWO OF THIS TASK'S STATED CRITERIA WERE OBSOLETE and were NOT chased (same correction task 070 made):
    the God-class LOC ratchet was retired 2026-08-20 (commit 866f9c101), so "under 2,000 lines" is no longer a
    gate, and `GodClassGuardTests.cs` DOES NOT EXIST -- there was no waiver to delete. Binding criterion applied
    instead, per root CLAUDE.md 11.5 / COMPONENT-COMPLEXITY.md: extract each cluster with its own reason to
    change, and state that reason per unit. The decomposition is justified on that standard's own terms -- the
    file held TWO independent output pipelines sharing only OOXML reading primitives, which is the low-cohesion
    signal the standard names -- not on line count.

    THE POML'S GUESSED SEAMS WERE WRONG. "block projection, run projection, atom identification, table
    projection, numbering, part traversal": block/run/table projection each exist TWICE, once per pipeline, so
    cutting along them would have halved both pipelines and left the halves coupled. Numbering and atom
    identification survived the guess. The dominant seam -- the pipeline boundary -- was not named.

    EQUIVALENCE: proven empirically after EACH extraction, never batched -- 25 corpus documents x both entry
    points, byte-identical all four times plus a final whole-task run. The oracle was itself validated on four
    axes BEFORE being trusted (deterministic; non-vacuous at 33 Success / 17 Partial / zero Failed; sensitive on
    BOTH pipelines via two separately-seeded mutations; restores to baseline). It was deleted on landing --
    scaffolding, per its own contract; resurrect recipe in the seam map.

    NEGATIVE criteria all verified: DI diff EMPTY (ADR-010); `Descendants&lt;Paragraph&gt;()` count 5 -> 5 (none
    introduced, none removed); `ProjectRun` capture set identical (Bold/Italic/Underline); no defect fixed
    silently -- none was found. Public API unchanged.

    Suites: BFF 11,683/0 - ArchTests 153/153 - build 0 errors 0 warnings. Publish 43.90 MB compressed incl PDBs
    (ceiling 60). No new NuGet; no new HIGH CVE. /conflict-check: silent pass (PR #887 touches ComposeService.cs
    -- the FROZEN file -- not this one).

    NOT DONE, DELIBERATELY: the planned fifth split (thin facade vs HTML pipeline). After the four extractions
    the remainder IS the HTML projection -- one pipeline, one reason to change. Splitting further would
    manufacture a class whose only purpose is to be small, the exact anti-pattern COMPONENT-COMPLEXITY.md
    replaced the ratchet to stop. Recorded as a 11.5 documented decision.

    Evidence: projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/071-projection-builder-seam-map.md
  </notes>
</task>
